  "term": "gap detection",
  "definition": "Gap detection is a perceptual measure of tactile sensitivity: the ability to notice a brief pause in an ongoing vibration applied to the skin. In this context, it is used to assess how well a person detects a short interruption in sustained vibrotactile stimulation.",
